{
  "id": "rae",
  "term": "RAE",
  "definition": "RAE stands for relative age effect, a pattern in age-grouped selection systems where children born earlier in the selection period are more likely to be seen as more talented because of early physical, cognitive, or behavioural advantages. Those early advantages can be amplified over time by selection decisions, greater access to coaching and practice, and differences in confidence or dropout.",
